From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:18:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: sun4i-gpadc: add a hwmon interface for the
 thermal zone

The GPADC of the Allwinner A10, A13 and A20 holds the SoC's only
temperature sensor, which the driver registers as the "cpu-thermal"
zone from the device tree. Device tree zones get no hwmon interface.
The MFD also instantiates an iio_hwmon device for the temperature
channel, but only kernels with CONFIG_SENSORS_IIO_HWMON get it
(multi_v7_defconfig has it, sunxi_defconfig does not), and it appears
as a generic "iio_hwmon" chip that tools cannot tell from any other IIO
temperature. So libsensors-based tools like sensors or htop's CPU
temperature either miss the SoC temperature or do not know it is one.

Register the zone's hwmon interface as sun8i_thermal does for the newer
Allwinner SoCs. It is named after the zone, "cpu_thermal", like the
zones of other ARM SoCs, which tools already recognise. With
CONFIG_SENSORS_IIO_HWMON the temperature is now listed twice, once per
interface.

Tested on an A10 board (Rikomagic MK802, without SENSORS_IIO_HWMON):
cpu_thermal appears with the zone's reading and htop shows the CPU
temperature.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c b/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c
index 1ee3da9ba..bb9926d7f 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/sun4i-gpadc-iio.c
@@ -666,6 +666,15 @@ static int sun4i_gpadc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			if (ret)
 				goto err_map;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * Device tree thermal zones get no hwmon interface by default.
+		 * Optional: the helper warns on its own if it fails. Keep this
+		 * after the zone and its release action: devres runs in
+		 * reverse order, and the hwmon device must go first.
+		 */
+		if (!IS_ERR(info->tzd))
+			devm_thermal_add_hwmon_sysfs(&pdev->dev, info->tzd);
 	}
 
 	ret = devm_iio_device_register(&pdev->dev, indio_dev);
-- 
